    review_mode: full
    review_visible: true
    writing_visible: true
    venue: CoRL 2026
    focus: 'Key risks: (1) Phase 0 classification too easy — does routing actually
      help downstream? (2) Single backbone pi0 generalizability. (3) Absolute performance
      vs SRPO/VLA-GSE SOTA. (4) 3-class taxonomy coarseness. Strongest evidence: Phase
      0 K=1 layer6 F1=1.0 proves zero-overhead routing. Core question for Claim 2:
      does specialized LoRA outperform universal LoRA?'
    what_if: []
